   approach="Row 30 has 2²⁹ symbols, so building it is out. Instead, notice that symbol k of row n is a **child** of symbol ⌈k/2⌉ of row n − 1. The left child (odd k) copies its parent; the right child (even k) is its flip.\n\nSo ask the recursion for the parent, then copy or flip it. One call per row.",
